Data in this folder

1. thai_readings.txt, thai_readings_full.tsv, thai_bound_forms.txt, thai_origins.txt, suspect_readings.tsv,
   pali_thai_script.txt

   License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   Attribution: derived from Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org and https://th.wiktionary.org), by Wiktionary
   contributors, via the wiktextract extractions published at https://kaikki.org/
   (Tatu Ylonen, "Wiktextract: Wiktionary as Machine-Readable Structured Data", LREC 2022).
   Snapshot: kaikki.org dumps dated 2026-09-28.

   Changes made: the pronunciation fields ("Phonemic" / "phoneme" and "bound form") were extracted; the pinthu mark
   and Wiktionary's shortened-vowel mark stacked with a tone mark were removed; syllables are joined by "-"; the two
   Wiktionary editions were merged (English Wiktionary first); readings failing a plausibility check were moved to
   suspect_readings.tsv; etymologies were reduced to a source-language tag (only stated borrowings);
   a "changed" flag was computed. pali_thai_script.txt: Thai-script word forms taken from Wiktionary Pali entries;
   their readings are generated by rules (thai_read.pali_reading) and are NOT from Wiktionary.

   If you share or adapt this data you must give appropriate credit, indicate changes, and distribute your
   contributions under the same license (CC BY-SA 4.0).

2. common_words.txt

   The 2,500 most frequent words of the Thai National Corpus word-frequency list as published by the PyThaiNLP
   project (pythainlp/corpus/tnc_freq.txt), released by PyThaiNLP under CC0 1.0 Universal
   (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). Only the order is used (no counts are included).

3. abbreviations.txt, keep_as_written.txt, my_readings.txt

   Original to this project; CC BY-SA 4.0 like the rest of data/.
